1
00:00:00,725 --> 00:00:09,163
[nd]: So, the pressure of restraint can sometimes make the mind irrational.

2
00:00:09,901 --> 00:00:18,216
[nd]: So, do you have any advice for how to maintain perspective in the face of the irrational mind?

3
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:29,525
[nm]: Well, maintaining perspective... it's gonna require you losing perspective, so to speak.

4
00:00:30,152 --> 00:00:32,320
[nm]: Maintaining perspective means developing perspective.

5
00:00:33,834 --> 00:00:41,390
[nm]: So, you can... you can know what the perspective is, but when the irrational mind is pressuring you, you're going to lose it.

6
00:00:42,503 --> 00:00:45,814
[nm]: Because otherwise, you wouldn't be pressured, or as not as pressured.

7
00:00:46,374 --> 00:00:56,565
[nm]: So, that's why it does boil down to then not acting out of the irrational mind... and feeling that grain that's trying to pull you with... to go with it

8
00:00:57,534 --> 00:01:03,290
[nm]: And trying to then exert the right perspective within it.

9
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:09,460
[nm]: So, it's not like, oh, I need to get the right perspective for this to go away.

10
00:01:09,854 --> 00:01:12,054
[nm]: More like, no, no, no, this won't be going away,

11
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:18,217
[nm]: the only thing I can and should be doing is have the perspective present with it.

12
00:01:18,854 --> 00:01:20,422
[nm]: That's how it eventually goes away.

13
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:25,477
[nm]: So, really... and that's not terribly hard to do...

14
00:01:26,442 --> 00:01:28,754
[nm]: What's kind of hard to not forget is to...

15
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:32,600
[nm]: fall back into the expectation for this pain to go away.

16
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:44,400
[nm]: And then, whether you're doing a perspective or this, or not acting out as well, you're doing it all under this intention of... so that it goes away.

17
00:01:44,997 --> 00:01:46,240
[nm]: And that's why it's not going away.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,140
[nm]: It won't go away because of that very reason.

19
00:01:49,148 --> 00:01:49,825
[nm]: So, it's like...

20
00:01:50,308 --> 00:01:53,585
[nm]: So, it's then more practically...

21
00:01:54,308 --> 00:01:56,402
[nm]: It's better, from a practical point of view, to then...

22
00:01:56,742 --> 00:01:57,154
[nm]: No, no, no.

23
00:01:57,174 --> 00:01:58,688
[nm]: It's not about it going away.

24
00:01:58,748 --> 00:02:00,034
[nm]: I don't want it to go away.

25
00:02:00,634 --> 00:02:07,148
[nm]: I want it to stay here, so that I can present it with a perspective, and then keep it there for as long as it's there.

26
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,637
[nm]: It's like as we said before, like a screaming child:

27
00:02:12,351 --> 00:02:16,631
[nm]: you can do this or that to appease it, so it stops screaming, or you could just

28
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:19,380
[nm]: Repeat how things are.

29
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:22,205
[nm]: The actual tell it that, no, this is how it is.

30
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:23,688
[nm]: And it refuses to hear that,

31
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:24,985
[nm]: it continues to scream,

32
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:28,125
[nm]: and you just hold the picture in front of it until it calms down and accepts it.

33
00:02:33,082 --> 00:02:35,245
[nd]: Or the knocking at the door.

34
00:02:36,094 --> 00:02:37,437
[nm]: Yeah, exactly... oh!

35
00:02:37,514 --> 00:02:39,797
[nm]: It's like, but hold on, why am I bothered?

36
00:02:39,797 --> 00:02:42,348
[nm]: Well, I'm bothered because I do still

37
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:50,185
[nm]: carry an assumption that it shouldn't be happening ,and it shouldn't be anybody in front of my door because... it would be better if it's not.

38
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,045
[nm]: So, I want it to not be in front of my door.

39
00:02:53,042 --> 00:02:54,388
[nm]: It's like, yeah, but that's not up to you.

40
00:02:55,891 --> 00:03:05,300
[nm]: So, the only reason you're resisting, or you're still pressured by somebody in front of your door, is because you still carry expectation that I want it to go away from in front of my door.

41
00:03:05,305 --> 00:03:07,325
[nm]: I want front of my door to be free and open.

42
00:03:08,154 --> 00:03:09,880
[nm]: It's like, but that's not your domain.

43
00:03:13,737 --> 00:03:34,837
[nd]: What if... so... because you start from this position of ignorance and you're just like... sometimes you're even like not aware maybe that you are like subtly, I don't know, opening the door somehow without...

44
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:36,502
[nm]: Well... there's no reason to mystify it like that.

45
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:41,137
[nm]: There's no reason to mystify it like that.

46
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:42,351
[nd]: There's always.

47
00:03:42,502 --> 00:03:45,505
[nm]: Even if it's true to some extent, it's irrelevant, really.

48
00:03:45,510 --> 00:03:47,608
[nm]: What's relevant is the stuff that you are aware of.

49
00:03:48,537 --> 00:03:55,980
[nm]: Yes, then later on you might find, oh, there are those other subtle ways, but to assume the subtle ways now are responsible for this, they're not.

50
00:03:56,644 --> 00:03:57,044
[nm]: They're not.

51
00:03:57,057 --> 00:03:58,088
[nm]: It's what you're doing now.

52
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:02,717
[nm]: Are you now still carrying the heavy assumption:

53
00:04:02,717 --> 00:04:05,457
[nm]: Mmm... No, I refuse to live under this.

54
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:07,525
[nm]: I want it to go away from the front of my door.

55
00:04:07,528 --> 00:04:08,868
[nm]: I don't want it to be there.

56
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:10,751
[nm]: That's really the problem.

57
00:04:17,094 --> 00:04:31,117
[nm]: So, it's the whole training that boils down to maintaining the perspective, or presenting the perspective, or reminding yourself of the right perspective, in face of that pain that has arisen on account of that irrational pressure.

58
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:37,542
[tj]: But, could you say that you'd be holding up that picture to the child?

59
00:04:39,085 --> 00:04:40,608
[tj]: But, you know, it's not for the child.

60
00:04:40,865 --> 00:04:46,377
[tj]: You know, the child could scream forever, but it's for you to remember as well.

61
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:52,424
[nm]: Well, it's for you to remember for sure, but fundamentally it's so that the child eventually learns.

62
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,043
[??]: Yeah.

63
00:04:53,777 --> 00:04:55,986
[nm]: Like, you can't help but want pain to go away.

64
00:04:56,069 --> 00:04:56,309
[??]: Yeah.

65
00:04:56,848 --> 00:04:59,130
[nm]: But you can certainly make sure that it's not

66
00:04:59,575 --> 00:05:02,946
[nm]: the root of your immediate intention, like: but I want it now.

67
00:05:02,946 --> 00:05:03,965
[nm]: Whatever I do, I want.

68
00:05:03,965 --> 00:05:06,459
[nm]: Like, yeah, you practice because you want to be free from suffering.

69
00:05:06,462 --> 00:05:06,761
[??]: Yeah.

70
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:18,737
[nm]: But not in that sense of through that denial, but through the sense of, no, no, I will be free from suffering when the mind stops or loses the ability to become irrational and turn against me and itself.

71
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:52,379
[nm]: But you could say... you could, like... if you practice this for a while, so you're not acting out, and then pressure comes and goes, sometimes more, sometimes less, sometimes better, sometimes worse, but overall, you're not sliding back in terms of your unwholesome actions, you're not going against the precepts, you're not losing sense restraint...

72
00:05:53,102 --> 00:06:01,537
[nm]: as I said, sometimes you more accurately re-establish perspective, sometimes that's just feel like too much work and you're just weathering it until it stops.

73
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,453
[nm]: You have to go through some extent of that.

74
00:06:05,878 --> 00:06:06,702
[nm]: It's inevitable.

75
00:06:07,550 --> 00:06:16,744
[nm]: But as you're doing it, as I said, even if you're just not acting out, but even if you don't have any perspective at the time, it's still obviously a form of staying with it.

76
00:06:17,753 --> 00:06:19,290
[nm]: It's not like, oh, this is wrong now.

77
00:06:19,293 --> 00:06:19,613
[nm]: No.

78
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,933
[nm]: There is no wrong for as long as you don't act out of it.

79
00:06:22,546 --> 00:06:26,911
[nm]: As long as the door is not open, there is nothing wrong what you do inside.

80
00:06:27,596 --> 00:06:32,859
[nm]: Yes, it's not the best thing you should do, but it's nowhere near the threshold of it's wrong.

81
00:06:33,913 --> 00:06:36,166
[nm]: Because that's another trick to get you to open the door.

82
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,643
[nm]: Well, it's wrong; I might as well open the door now.

83
00:06:40,368 --> 00:06:43,610
[nm]: But for as long as the door is not open, it's not wrong.

84
00:06:43,613 --> 00:06:44,128
[nm]: It's not wrong.

85
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,033
[nm]: It simply isn't.

86
00:06:45,186 --> 00:06:45,680
[nm]: It cannot be.

87
00:06:46,107 --> 00:06:46,935
[nd]: No matter how much...

88
00:06:46,931 --> 00:06:51,673
[nm]: It doesn't matter how confused, how doubtful, how everything else you might be feeling.

89
00:06:51,676 --> 00:06:53,109
[nm]: It's like, yeah, but the door's not open.

90
00:06:54,657 --> 00:06:55,102
[nm]: So...

91
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:56,932
[nm]: It's still better than being open.

92
00:06:57,238 --> 00:07:02,403
[nm]: So, it's still more right than it would have been otherwise.

93
00:07:05,203 --> 00:07:15,565
[tj]: Is... is that the clarity about what that doorway is... always available?

94
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:19,224
[nm]: Well, whenever there is a pressure, there's a doorway.

95
00:07:21,102 --> 00:07:24,528
[tj]: Like the... the line of... because you can...

96
00:07:25,129 --> 00:07:26,070
[tj]: You lose sight of that.

97
00:07:26,504 --> 00:07:27,979
[tn]: Yeah, right, yeah.

98
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:29,426
[tj]: But...

99
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:31,589
[nm]: Yeah, so...

100
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,706
[tj]: It's the recollection of that.

101
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,158
[nm]: It's...

102
00:07:33,175 --> 00:07:37,610
[nm]: I think, let's say, the doorway is basically if you... if you, like, really act out of it.

103
00:07:39,933 --> 00:07:46,083
[nm]: So, you could be walking towards the door, be on the other side of the door, but not open it.

104
00:07:46,991 --> 00:07:53,523
[nm]: Obviously, if you are constantly just sitting on the other side of the door next to the door handle, well, the pressure to open it will increase.

105
00:07:54,556 --> 00:07:56,045
[nm]: So, you need to recognize that as well.

106
00:07:56,360 --> 00:08:00,987
[nm]: But, fundamentally, as long as you don't open it, you are safe, even if it doesn't feel like that.

107
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,893
[nm]: And it won't feel like that, because that's the only true safety.

108
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,822
[nm]: That's what the Māra would presented it as: no, no, no.

109
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:12,991
[nm]: This is the worst thing you can do.

110
00:08:12,994 --> 00:08:13,756
[nm]: Don't do this.

111
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:21,558
[nm]: But you could, that's... and that's something in that part, when you're on the inside,

112
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:33,777
[nm]: of the house, when you're not opening the door, but you are kind of getting, like, walking past the door, examining the door, thinking about opening the door, trying to all this.

113
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:36,201
[nm]: You realize, okay, I could stop that now.

114
00:08:36,730 --> 00:08:42,629
[nm]: And that's that part we talked about before, of, like, not allowing images to take the center stage.

115
00:08:43,676 --> 00:08:52,034
[nm]: And as we said also, I think, in one of the talks, it's like, even without them being the center stage, you already know what they are.

116
00:08:53,231 --> 00:09:00,309
[nm]: So, even if I don't explicitly start thinking about things: I'm being pressured and all this and that... if I were to allow it, I know exactly what I will think.

117
00:09:01,158 --> 00:09:02,560
[nm]: So, it's like, so, I won't.

118
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:03,996
[nm]: I won't allow it in the center stage.

119
00:09:04,006 --> 00:09:06,563
[nm]: Again, I'm not trying to get rid of who is in front of the door.

120
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:12,208
[nm]: I'm not trying to get rid of all these thoughts that are... that would be associated with it.

121
00:09:12,563 --> 00:09:14,560
[nm]: I'm just keeping them into that blur.

122
00:09:14,869 --> 00:09:18,660
[nm]: I'm not allowing them to crystallize through my own efforts.

123
00:09:20,285 --> 00:09:21,993
[nm]: If they pop up on their own, that's fine.

124
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:26,803
[nm]: That's a completely different thing than if they pop up because I intended them to do so.

125
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:28,539
[nm]: Although it feels the same.

126
00:09:28,550 --> 00:09:29,916
[nm]: The end result feels the same.

127
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,617
[nm]: It's the same image that popped up.

128
00:09:32,027 --> 00:09:34,194
[nm]: But one came through your own intention, one didn't.

129
00:09:34,998 --> 00:09:37,735
[nm]: If it's through your own intention, that's the center stage I talk about.

130
00:09:38,956 --> 00:09:43,304
[nm]: And that's actually... there's a whole universe of difference between the tw,.

131
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:45,293
[nm]: but you need to arrive at it.

132
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,542
[nm]: The difference is internal.

133
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:51,746
[nm]: It's not in the content of the image...

134
00:09:51,753 --> 00:09:56,170
[nm]: and the center stage, that remains the same, but it's how it go there means

135
00:09:56,330 --> 00:09:59,405
[nm]: whether there is the five aggregates with upadana, or without.

136
00:10:00,417 --> 00:10:09,283
[nm]: And eventually if you do not allow the center stage, there will be no five aggregates. There will be the complete cessation of anything that was activated.

137
00:10:13,485 --> 00:10:19,046
[nm]: It's like, I don't know if I said in another talk, or just speaking, without recording... it's like

138
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:34,285
[nm]: imagine you have like a, like a, like a, I don't know, a place with a glass in between, that is just like a, I don't know, a square meter of foot space, and there is like a transparent glass in between.

139
00:10:34,344 --> 00:10:35,836
[nm]: So it's like this on the same spot.

140
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:45,603
[nm]: But the only way to get from one side of that glass, like 10 centimeters, well, not even 10, like one centimeter on the other side of the glass,

141
00:10:45,870 --> 00:10:51,175
[nm]: you have to go all the way around, completely, all the way around, to a different world, to arrive at the same thing.

142
00:10:51,186 --> 00:10:54,793
[nm]: It looks the same. You still look at the same thing that's there, on that floor.

143
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:58,608
[nm]: And that's this. That's exactly it.

144
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:00,890
[nm]: So you have the images and stuff that present themselves...

145
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:08,264
[nm]: untrained mind wouldn't see a difference between picking them up with your intention, and them coming up on their own.

146
00:11:09,321 --> 00:11:13,846
[nm]: And then it would think, I need to deal with the content, I need to deal with the thoughts themselves...

147
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:18,267
[nm]: It's like, no, you need to deal with your intention in thinking them.

148
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:25,885
[nm]: And that's that practice of not allowing them the center stage while the blurry cloud is there waiting to crystallize.

149
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:28,570
[nm]: But if it crystallizes on its own, you're free.

150
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:29,332
[nm]: You're still free.

151
00:11:29,867 --> 00:11:31,008
[nm]: You're untouched by it.

152
00:11:31,826 --> 00:11:36,514
[nm]: If it crystallizes through your own intention of picking it up, that's what touches you.

153
00:11:39,283 --> 00:11:42,187
[nm]: And that's the practice that can only be done indoors.

154
00:11:43,026 --> 00:11:48,281
[nm]: You can only do this practice and eventually discern this difference if the door remains closed.

155
00:11:49,238 --> 00:11:56,274
[nm]: If you go out to deal with stuff that's in front of your door, through your techniques and managements and stuff, none of this will be applicable.

156
00:11:56,306 --> 00:11:57,965
[nm]: This domain ceases to exist.

157
00:12:01,158 --> 00:12:02,671
[nd]: The distinction between those two?

158
00:12:02,750 --> 00:12:11,523
[nm]: Well, the distinction theoretically remains, but practical possibility of seeing it is gone.

159
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:16,862
[nm]: Because you need to close the door for those distinctions to start to appear.

160
00:12:26,690 --> 00:12:31,206
[nm]: That's like... So, imagine now... Say you're not... You're... You're...

161
00:12:31,255 --> 00:12:32,550
[nm]: There's a hindrance pressuring you.

162
00:12:32,570 --> 00:12:39,231
[nm]: Whether it's the doubt, ill-will, sensuality... You know the state of mind.

163
00:12:39,234 --> 00:12:41,641
[nm]: You know the general cloud that's waiting there...

164
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:45,193
[nm]: pressuring you to start intentionally crystallizing the thoughts.

165
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:50,660
[nm]: So, if you refrain... Again, I don't need to be cancelling the mind.

166
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:56,806
[nm]: That's the painful part, when you think you need to be changing this weight and the direction of this weather...

167
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:58,257
[nm]: and that's impossible.

168
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,892
[nm]: But you don't actually... I don't have to do that.

169
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:06,626
[nm]: The sole reason that any of that would be a problem is if I'm making a connection, creating a connection,

170
00:13:07,270 --> 00:13:12,313
[nm]: activation through intentionally crystallizing thoughts that are being pushed at me.

171
00:13:14,838 --> 00:13:21,596
[nm]: So, if you are not allowing them the center stage... Say there is a mind that pressures you towards, I don't know, thoughts of ill will.

172
00:13:23,537 --> 00:13:24,493
[nm]: Somebody knows you.

173
00:13:24,834 --> 00:13:29,739
[nm]: If you were to intentionally now go towards those thoughts, you know exactly what you will think.

174
00:13:29,812 --> 00:13:34,608
[nm]: But you're not doing that, so the pressure is there, but there is no specific thoughts of hatred that come from you.

175
00:13:35,798 --> 00:13:37,321
[nm]: What are you left with there and then?

176
00:13:38,295 --> 00:13:46,914
[nm]: Like, in your state, like, even imagine now, whatever subtle pressure you might be feeling on account of some hindrance, you're not allowing the center stage in regard to that very pressure.

177
00:13:47,370 --> 00:13:48,619
[nm]: What are you left with then, now?

178
00:13:50,584 --> 00:13:52,290
[nd]: The pressure with.

179
00:13:53,106 --> 00:13:56,657
[nm]: Yeah, of course, the pressure is there, but broadly speaking...

180
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,525
[nm]: I mean, your body... is there...

181
00:13:58,528 --> 00:14:00,130
[nm]:  Just basically here and now.

182
00:14:00,163 --> 00:14:01,290
[nm]: You're left with here and now.

183
00:14:01,290 --> 00:14:01,353
[nd]: Yeah.
[nm]: You're left with here and now.

184
00:14:01,353 --> 00:14:01,662
[nd]: Yeah.

185
00:14:02,486 --> 00:14:08,577
[nm]: So, you're not... and that here and now, there, it's not being thought through a taken-up pressure.

186
00:14:09,471 --> 00:14:13,161
[nm]: It's what you're left with by not allowing intentions to take up the pressure.

187
00:14:13,415 --> 00:14:17,572
[md]: And if you start, like, thinking it as a way to...

188
00:14:17,610 --> 00:14:27,067
[nm]: Yeah, I was gonna say that... and that's why, like, sometimes people would then think, aha, so I'll think here and now to not act out of the pressure. It's like, but that's now your pressure.

189
00:14:27,641 --> 00:14:29,813
[nm]: So, although it's the same here and now,

190
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:33,836
[nm]: you arrived at it completely from the opposite directions.

191
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:39,809
[nm]: The here and now that you often hear about, it's like you focus, you get to it, you get to it, you get to it.

192
00:14:40,198 --> 00:14:42,563
[nm]: It's like, no, the here and now is what you are left with.

193
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:47,062
[nm]: And you could see how it was maybe right at some point, to some degree, with somebody...

194
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:58,636
[nm]: they arrived at it rightly, and then they mystify the here and now, and then subsequently, as that has been repeated thousands of times, people forgot the whole context of the actual travel

195
00:14:58,891 --> 00:15:00,609
[nm]: and journey to it, right one,

196
00:15:01,131 --> 00:15:02,998
[nm]: and then they just start, no, just here and now.

197
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:04,194
[nm]: Nibbāna is already here.

198
00:15:04,201 --> 00:15:05,123
[nm]: There's nothing to do.

199
00:15:05,123 --> 00:15:06,003
[nm]: Just focus on it.

200
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:09,752
[nm]: Just stop this, just, just... just kind of be present and all of that.

201
00:15:10,194 --> 00:15:11,401
[nm]: And it's like what I said:

202
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:16,000
[nm]: it's like you you remain on this sheet of glass because the other one, the other side remains identical, looks identical.

203
00:15:16,007 --> 00:15:17,302
[nm]: So you see no difference.

204
00:15:17,950 --> 00:15:25,996
[nm]: But there is a difference whether you are in left with here and now, through your concentration practice of being here and now,

205
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:30,636
[nm]: or through simply not allowing the crystalization of the pressuring thoughts. So, here and now is the result.

206
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,205
[tj]: So, through, through restrain...

207
00:15:38,921 --> 00:15:41,878
[nm]: Yeah, so here and now is the result. It's not something you do.

208
00:15:41,923 --> 00:15:43,367
[nm]: It's the result of something you do.

209
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:51,912
[nm]: And you can't just, through a shortcut, just focus on here and now and bypass the world.

210
00:15:53,455 --> 00:15:55,946
[nm]: Because that will be taken up in the same way.

211
00:15:59,009 --> 00:16:01,386
[tj]: So, you might... it might be...

212
00:16:02,221 --> 00:16:02,981
[tj]: I don't know...

213
00:16:03,001 --> 00:16:11,107
[tj]: Simultaneously, you're asking a question, like, at the right time, and then, to regain perspective.

214
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:16,636
[tj]: And then, you latch on to that, asking a question, and that becomes your method.

215
00:16:16,650 --> 00:16:18,685
[nm]: Your method, yeah. You just start doing it blindly, yeah.

216
00:16:18,692 --> 00:16:21,434
[tj]: And you don't see that it was just a refrain.

217
00:16:21,430 --> 00:16:23,116
[nm]: It happens, yeah. It's inevitable.

218
00:16:23,116 --> 00:16:26,099
[nm]: Like, you will be doing it to a degree.

219
00:16:26,281 --> 00:16:28,453
[nm]: It's not going to be perfect the first time.

220
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:37,912
[nm]: But that's why the instruction has to remain unobscured and keep pointing you and you keep reminding yourself of where the actual emphasis and the right work is.

221
00:16:38,552 --> 00:16:50,636
[nm]: So, you start... you ask a question at the right time, you establish the perspective, you don't allow the pressuring, you know, peripheral cloud of thoughts to crystallize through your own ignorant efforts.

222
00:16:50,963 --> 00:16:51,462
[nm]: But then...

223
00:16:52,150 --> 00:17:00,685
[nm]: you slip, you get caught in it, but then when you catch yourself that that's what you've been doing, you know, like, okay, but now that needs to be included rightly.

224
00:17:01,398 --> 00:17:04,746
[nm]: Now, in regard to that, I don't repeat the same mistake.

225
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:09,779
[nm]: Or I try to, like, foresee it before it's... before I allow it.

226
00:17:11,657 --> 00:17:12,994
[nm]: And that's how you progress.

227
00:17:13,653 --> 00:17:18,475
[nm]: But if you catch yourself and then you think, oh, but this is actually not a problem, that's it.

228
00:17:19,401 --> 00:17:22,457
[nm]: That's why the wrong view is the worst possible thing a person can do.

229
00:17:23,706 --> 00:17:25,466
[nm]: Like, even from the saṃsāra point of view.

230
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:29,878
[nm]: Because, for that sole reason, you won't stay on the right level.

231
00:17:30,373 --> 00:17:35,817
[nm]: You won't endure the pressure of somebody in front of your door on the right level, because you would think you don't have to.

232
00:17:40,110 --> 00:17:41,405
[nm]: And that's another thing: see...

233
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:44,579
[nm]: See, you have somebody pressuring you to open the door,

234
00:17:46,270 --> 00:17:53,398
[nm]: you've been panicking inside, and moving, and getting closer, or going away, or trying to cement the door, or, looking, throw a bomb outside... Well, it doesn't matter.

235
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:58,076
[nm]: And then, eventually, you sort of calm down, because you recognize, yeah, it's still, but the point is the door is not open.

236
00:17:58,087 --> 00:18:01,169
[nm]: So, why don't I calm down these thoughts while I'm inside?

237
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:05,405
[nm]: And you calm them down, again, not through denial, not through wishing there's nobody from the door.

238
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:11,142
[nm]: Just... just let me not have that last say in their crystallization.

239
00:18:11,154 --> 00:18:15,836
[nm]: Just keep my mind free from those images in the center stage, while they're there.

240
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:17,958
[nm]: How do you know they're there?

241
00:18:17,970 --> 00:18:21,219
[nm]: Well, allow the center stage, you know exactly what's going to come even before it comes.

242
00:18:21,222 --> 00:18:22,422
[nm]: So, you know they're there.

243
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:26,380
[nm]: You know what they are... already, even without thinking them explicitly.

244
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:30,864
[nm]: And then, you realize you do that and then the pressure can't touch you.

245
00:18:31,055 --> 00:18:35,805
[nm]: Then, you can have hundred many people in front of the door or creatures trying to pressure you to open it.

246
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:42,312
[nm]: The only reason you were pressured is when those images were taking the center stage through your own ignorant intention of placing them there.

247
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:56,601
[nm]: That's why Arahant's behavior is... there is no measurable, imperceivable difference between private and public.

248
00:18:58,152 --> 00:18:58,933
[nm]: It's the same.

249
00:18:59,310 --> 00:19:04,270
[nm]: As in private, he's so in public, as in public, he's in private. There is no... there's no change there.

250
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:17,017
[nd]: Well, just to go back to this example, let's say, eh... there's a question,

251
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:24,998
[nd]: But it is the case that, in that moment, there is a sense of anxiety...

252
00:19:26,530 --> 00:19:37,158
[nd]: and there is a sense of, maybe, like, obligation or, yeah, that I need to ask a question right now.

253
00:19:39,725 --> 00:19:44,880
[nd]: That, yeah, opening the door.

254
00:19:45,653 --> 00:19:48,899
[nd]: It's to act out of that, to ignore that...

255
00:19:49,066 --> 00:19:49,740
[nm]: But that's a subtle...

256
00:19:49,748 --> 00:19:51,207
[nm]: I mean, not... yeah, not quite.

257
00:19:51,203 --> 00:19:54,213
[nm]: It's kind of coming to the door handle and...

258
00:19:55,508 --> 00:19:57,900
[nm]: But it wouldn't really be opening the door.

259
00:19:57,992 --> 00:20:06,963
[nm]: Opening the door is when you act, because the pressure... the hindrances are not going to pressure you towards learning more about the dhamma or something.

260
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:12,377
[nm]: Your desperate efforts might go in that direction, because you still try to get rid of who's in front of the door.

261
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:18,487
[nm]: But, fundamentally, opening the door is, you know, when you act towards the pressures.

262
00:20:19,323 --> 00:20:20,223
[nm]: When you really give in.

263
00:20:20,224 --> 00:20:23,969
[nm]: So, as I said, as long as that's not done, you're still safe.

264
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:29,900
[nm]: But then, yes, of course, once you become confident in that, you could realize, yeah, but I don't even have to think about the door.

265
00:20:31,459 --> 00:20:32,205
[nm]: It's not a problem.

266
00:20:32,243 --> 00:20:34,316
[nm]: I don't even have to think about who's in front of the door.

267
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:35,062
[nm]: That's not a problem.

268
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:43,436
[nm]: The only problem is that I am pressured here and now, through, intentionally, through ignorant intentions, allowing those images, associated with it, to take the center stage.

269
00:20:45,112 --> 00:20:48,575
[nm]: Again, it's kind of... it sounds like it can easily become on that level.

270
00:20:48,579 --> 00:20:50,000
[nm]: It's like, oh, I asked the question.

271
00:20:50,011 --> 00:20:51,630
[nm]: I acted out of it, didn't I?

272
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:52,274
[nm]: I made a...

273
00:20:52,278 --> 00:20:53,112
[nm]: It's a, it's a mistake.

274
00:20:53,287 --> 00:20:53,988
[nm]: Like, no, you  haven't.

275
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,659
[nm]: You're still inside, the door is still closed. You haven't acted out.

276
00:20:57,767 --> 00:21:00,899
[nm]: You haven't acted out of the major doubt and abandoned the training.

277
00:21:01,386 --> 00:21:05,436
[nm]: You haven't acted out on account of the hindrance of sensuality and broke the precepts.

278
00:21:05,904 --> 00:21:10,034
[nm]: You haven't acted out on account of anger and punched somebody or said something really, like, furious.

279
00:21:10,064 --> 00:21:10,731
[nm]: You haven't.

280
00:21:11,946 --> 00:21:15,546
[nm]: Yes, mentally, I've been getting to the door and wanting to do it or not.

281
00:21:15,809 --> 00:21:16,800
[nm]: That's the training.

282
00:21:18,662 --> 00:21:23,226
[nm]: Oh, yeah, and I've been asking these stupid questions this whole time, just really... That's the training.

283
00:21:23,672 --> 00:21:29,440
[nm]: Then, you get to recognize that as like, okay, now I refine it within the indoor environment.

284
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,156
[nm]: That's the point.

285
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:32,125
[nm]: There is still no opening of the door.

286
00:21:33,847 --> 00:21:35,160
[nm]: But it's not incidental.

287
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:41,459
[nm]: The mind wants to confuse you about what you do inside, so that that makes no difference whether the door is open or not.

288
00:21:41,836 --> 00:21:42,937
[nm]: Because that's how it's going to feel.

289
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:47,226
[nm]: Because there is a huge difference whether the door is open or not.

290
00:21:50,582 --> 00:22:09,577
[md]: I was going to say, like, because it's... acting out doesn't mean doing some action while there is a pressuring state of mind, because you have... you're going to be doing something while there is a pressuring state of mind.

291
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:19,939
[md]: It's whether what you're doing is, like, really rooted in that pressuring state of mind, as in, like, what it wants you to do.

292
00:22:21,379 --> 00:22:22,030
[md]: Opening the door.

293
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:24,640
[nm]: Even within that, yeah, even within that...

294
00:22:25,690 --> 00:22:30,586
[nm]: In the beginning, it will be like, the asking question might be rooted in the pressuring state of mind.

295
00:22:31,910 --> 00:22:32,556
[nm]: Let's see.

296
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:39,150
[nm]: It's still not on the level of opening the door for what you're obviously pressured towards.

297
00:22:40,636 --> 00:22:48,929
[nm]: So, it's going to be rooted, like, you pacing inside of your... of the room, with the door closed, and coming close to the door, and walking away...

298
00:22:48,937 --> 00:22:51,954
[nm]: it's all determined by the pressure at the outside of the door.

299
00:22:53,192 --> 00:22:54,130
[nm]: So, I'll just stop it.

300
00:22:54,133 --> 00:22:57,510
[nm]: Well, that will now be determined by the stuff that's in front of your door.

301
00:22:57,530 --> 00:22:59,302
[nm]: I'll just sit still, motionless.

302
00:22:59,634 --> 00:23:00,022
[nm]: Why?

303
00:23:00,198 --> 00:23:04,750
[nm]: Because there is a pressure that I'm under, because somebody's in front of my door trying to make me to open it.

304
00:23:05,721 --> 00:23:09,699
[nm]: Whatever you do will be rooted in it, but it's like, you recognize, okay,

305
00:23:12,270 --> 00:23:16,373
[nm]: by not allowing it to spill out, it's still contained.

306
00:23:17,268 --> 00:23:19,805
[nm]: And that's the training now, once it's contained.

307
00:23:20,620 --> 00:23:28,099
[nm]: And there is a difference between that, because, as I said, the whole point of Māra making you confused is so you see that there is no... you think there is no difference.

308
00:23:28,110 --> 00:23:30,316
[nm]: Oh, I'm confused in here, I might be confused in...

309
00:23:30,330 --> 00:23:31,645
[nm]: It doesn't matter, I might open the door.

310
00:23:31,935 --> 00:23:32,849
[nm]: It's like, no, no, no.

311
00:23:33,219 --> 00:23:35,051
[nm]: It's still a better type of confusion.

312
00:23:35,051 --> 00:23:36,377
[nm]: It's a better type of pain.

313
00:23:37,130 --> 00:23:39,036
[nm]: And that's what Buddha said: you should replace

314
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:42,594
[nm]: the happiness of household life with the happiness of renunciation,

315
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:47,409
[nm]: the happiness of outdoor projects with the happiness of indoor peace.

316
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:53,485
[nm]: You should replace the pain of the outdoor engagements with the pain of indoor pressure.

317
00:23:55,093 --> 00:23:56,929
[nm]: And then, eventually, you would abandon that too.

318
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:17,291
[md]: And is that also... is there something relevant there as well, about basically, kind of, prioritizing...

319
00:24:19,165 --> 00:24:29,535
[md]: I suppose, like, doing things in the right order, in terms of, like, prioritizing the things that you are clear about,

320
00:24:29,862 --> 00:24:43,481
[md]: Rather than trying to, for example, like you were talking about, once you're inside the door, then you can start, like, not allowing the images to crystallize, you know, so that you don't even have to do that part, and then you can be at peace...

321
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:49,196
[md]: and, you know, from the point of view of somebody who's, like, still fully, very much pressured, it's like, oh, that sounds very nice.

322
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:53,540
[md]: Let me quickly try and do that part, so as to not have to deal with it.

323
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:56,506
[md]: And actually, that won't work. You know, it's...

324
00:24:56,520 --> 00:24:57,946
[nm]: No, and you feel it: it doesn't work.

325
00:24:57,950 --> 00:25:00,163
[nm]: But the right information remains there.

326
00:25:00,163 --> 00:25:00,390
[md]: Yeah.

327
00:25:00,410 --> 00:25:04,118
[nm]: To be, eventually, to land on the right thing, if you keep doing it.

328
00:25:04,170 --> 00:25:04,891
[nm]: That's the point.

329
00:25:07,123 --> 00:25:07,565
[nm]: That's the point.

330
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:13,588
[nm]: But, no, definitely, there is... there is a whole sequence to this.

331
00:25:13,809 --> 00:25:18,960
[nm]: Because you could be trying to not allow the center stage while your door is freaking wide open.

332
00:25:19,379 --> 00:25:20,921
[nm]: And things just coming in and out.

333
00:25:21,588 --> 00:25:22,350
[nm]: Doesn't matter.

334
00:25:22,853 --> 00:25:25,352
[nm]: Actions, speech, doesn't matter.

335
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:31,607
[nm]: Like, yeah, you're just revolving around abstract ideas, even if you had the right instruction.

336
00:25:32,342 --> 00:25:40,228
[nm]: So, it's like, no, the training is, you gotta learn, like, for the door to remain closed.

337
00:25:41,558 --> 00:25:44,529
[nm]: And then, take on that.

338
00:25:44,872 --> 00:25:48,438
[nm]: It's gonna feel pressuring now, because before you used to roam around wherever you wanted.

339
00:25:48,982 --> 00:25:51,725
[nm]: It's like, yeah, but that's why you were prey to suffering wherever you went.

340
00:25:53,706 --> 00:25:54,864
[tj]: Is it also...

341
00:25:56,497 --> 00:26:00,539
[tj]: It's not just like, well, today the door was closed.

342
00:26:00,550 --> 00:26:03,074
[tj]: This week the door was closed... it's like

343
00:26:03,409 --> 00:26:04,860
[nm]: Yeah, it needs to stay closed.

344
00:26:04,921 --> 00:26:10,360
[tj]: Yeah, it needs to stay... and it's not like I do it now and then later.

345
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:14,982
[nm]: Yeah, I'll close it for, you know, five days, open it on the weekends or something.

346
00:26:14,994 --> 00:26:16,369
[nm]: Yeah... yeah...

347
00:26:16,899 --> 00:26:21,626
[nm]: I mean, I suppose if somebody is absolutely wild, assutavā, unrestrained,

348
00:26:22,220 --> 00:26:33,767
[nm]: it's... it could be a way to start, to eventually have your doors closed all the time, but you've got to recognize that there's nowhere near the necessary threshold for any successful practice.

349
00:26:34,186 --> 00:26:36,655
[nm]: But, yes, some people need to work towards the threshold.

350
00:26:37,810 --> 00:26:49,116
[nm]: But it's important to qualify this, because if you say, well, yes, start by having a door closed three or four days, they'll think, okay, by doing this absolute sub-par levels, I am also practicing the dhamma.

351
00:26:49,116 --> 00:26:52,396
[nm]: No, you're just getting closer to the level where you could start practicing the dhamma.

352
00:26:52,790 --> 00:26:57,207
[nm]: Which, of course, you could argue it's a formal practice, but it's not the dhamma practice.

353
00:26:57,211 --> 00:26:58,807
[nm]: It's like preparatory practice.

354
00:27:00,133 --> 00:27:04,274
[tj]: I've been thinking

355
00:27:06,090 --> 00:27:19,177
[tj]: kind of, maybe a rough marker, just to kind of, kind of gauge, to gauge where you're at, would be, yeah, what what what you're still opening, actually opening the door to.

356
00:27:19,250 --> 00:27:19,489
[nm]: Yeah.

357
00:27:19,798 --> 00:27:25,078
[tj]: Like your, like your work, your sort of worst moment, in a sense.

358
00:27:25,660 --> 00:27:26,940
[tj]: What you're still getting at.

359
00:27:26,975 --> 00:27:31,836
[nm]: What's, well, yeah, and then you might say, like, you're not opening the door, but you're still peeking through the curtains.

360
00:27:31,859 --> 00:27:33,657
[tj]: Yeah, right, yeah.

361
00:27:34,213 --> 00:27:37,520
[nm]: So, it's like, oh, hold on, but that means I'm still concerned.

362
00:27:37,870 --> 00:27:38,594
[tj]: Yeah.

363
00:27:38,933 --> 00:27:42,034
[nm]: I'm still pressured by the outside, so I'm still acting towards it.

364
00:27:42,064 --> 00:27:48,860
[nm]: Then you might not be peeking through the curtains, but as I said, you still come and you just, just, just think about pressing the handle, even if you know you're not going to do it.

365
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,822
[nm]: It's like... yeah, but why I am doing it like that?

366
00:27:51,650 --> 00:27:54,800
[nm]: So, that's that refinement of the purification of your thoughts.

367
00:27:55,371 --> 00:28:12,167
[nm]: And then, as I said, if you go in that direction, the distinction that I said between thoughts just popping up on their own in the center stage and thoughts being placed in the center stage through their own ignorant intention, it's the difference between saṃsāra and nibbāna, basically.

368
00:28:14,060 --> 00:28:14,689
[nm]: Nothing else.

369
00:28:14,788 --> 00:28:17,268
[nm]: It's like the root of all the problems.

370
00:28:40,963 --> 00:28:52,870
[tj]: And clarifying that, or clarifying this as well, just like the door, what acts as, what counts as acting out, to [??], is done practically.

371
00:28:54,224 --> 00:28:54,883
[nm]: No other way.

372
00:28:54,883 --> 00:28:55,900
[nm]: Yeah, no other way.

373
00:28:58,297 --> 00:29:09,977
[nm]: And yes, from the point of view of eventually not being moved by any pressure, when you think back, pacing inside of the room on account of the pressure was acting out.

374
00:29:10,220 --> 00:29:11,980
[nm]: But it wasn't acting out, acting out.

375
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:29,340
[tn]: Yes, say, if you... you press your [??], you... there's anger knocking at the door, and you don't open it, you care about it, and then you start to... you're just enduring that, and it's still there, and you're still... there's pain.

376
00:29:30,811 --> 00:29:39,131
[tn]: Well, I'll just keep knowing that it's at the door, examine it, discern it, and then the thought

377
00:29:40,049 --> 00:29:41,942
[tn]: Well, you just acted out there.

378
00:29:42,180 --> 00:29:44,346
[tn]: Your discernment is doing something, isn't it?

379
00:29:44,548 --> 00:29:46,681
[tn]: But that's... it is doing something.

380
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:48,160
[nm]: It is doing something, but...

381
00:29:48,170 --> 00:29:53,017
[tn]: It's a doing of the discernment of just reinforcing the fact that the door is closed.

382
00:29:53,017 --> 00:29:56,430
[nm]: It's... it's the simile of the purifying... purifying of the gold in the suttas.

383
00:29:56,457 --> 00:30:05,695
[nm]: You know, when you're purifying... when you're separating the coarse impurities from the liquid mass,

384
00:30:07,367 --> 00:30:12,582
[nm]: When you put aside the stuff you want to keep, you take lots of impurities with it, just not as coarse.

385
00:30:14,300 --> 00:30:19,820
[nm]: Then, when you start purifying that, you put further aside stuff you want to keep, it still contains all the impurities.

386
00:30:19,828 --> 00:30:24,460
[nm]: So, technically, you are still acting out, you are still taking on other impurities.

387
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:27,017
[nm]: Yeah, but at the expense of dropping a coarser one.

388
00:30:27,748 --> 00:30:35,916
[nm]: Because you can't be, as I said before, like with a tweezer, picking microscopic impurities in the gold, what is like a lump of excrement floating around.

389
00:30:36,453 --> 00:30:39,942
[nm]: It's just... well, that's like... makes absolutely no difference.

390
00:30:41,451 --> 00:30:45,100
[nm]: So, the problem is not like, oh, I acted out, I asked the question and I have to have this...

391
00:30:45,733 --> 00:30:49,500
[nm]: The problem is, then, whether you have perspective in regard to that.

392
00:30:52,180 --> 00:30:54,453
[nm]: So, like, yeah, but the door is not open.

393
00:30:55,337 --> 00:30:58,970
[nm]: It's not ideal, sure, but now I get perspective and I recognize that.

394
00:30:59,424 --> 00:31:01,074
[nm]: And there's already confidence born from it.

395
00:31:01,074 --> 00:31:04,544
[nm]: Okay, so I can think about it, even if it's out of pressure.

396
00:31:05,270 --> 00:31:08,369
[nm]: Because I'm not going towards the door, and I'm not thinking in terms of opening the door.

397
00:31:09,912 --> 00:31:13,177
[nm]: Then, eventually, you realize, but why am I even thinking about it, in that sense?

398
00:31:13,170 --> 00:31:17,607
[nm]: Why am I even allowing center stage for those thoughts to come forward, when I already know the answer?

399
00:31:18,426 --> 00:31:23,760
[nm]: It's just a compulsion, a pressure to allow it, to place itself, to crystallize itself.

400
00:31:23,767 --> 00:31:24,860
[nm]: So, I won't do even that.

401
00:31:27,196 --> 00:31:35,318
[nm]: And that's all, you know, even from the start, you know, when somebody shuts the door by taking on a life of the eight precepts,

402
00:31:36,430 --> 00:31:40,476
[nm]: and they finally shut their door, but then they hold it shut.

403
00:31:41,459 --> 00:31:46,712
[nm]: Every second of their life, they're leaning into the door and squeezing the handle so that it's not opened.

404
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:56,834
[nm]: And it's like, yeah, you might start like that, and probably many people would, but then you recognize, hold on, I don't need to hold it, because it can't be opened on its own.

405
00:31:58,450 --> 00:32:02,449
[nm]: The only way for that door to open, it cannot be open accidentally, nor open from the outside.

406
00:32:03,070 --> 00:32:05,440
[nm]: The only way to open it is me to actively open it.

407
00:32:06,045 --> 00:32:07,459
[nm]: So, you don't need to keep the precepts.

408
00:32:07,466 --> 00:32:08,887
[nm]: You just need to not break them.

409
00:32:11,740 --> 00:32:14,106
[nm]: But that in itself will cause doubt.

410
00:32:14,899 --> 00:32:16,929
[nm]: They will then blur the line where the door is.

411
00:32:17,432 --> 00:32:31,497
[nm]: And if people even allow, people that are still dependent on gripping the door out of fear, and feeling justified in doing so, if you tell them you gotta let go of the door, for them, that's like saying you have to open it and go and dance with what's in front of the door.

412
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:33,260
[nm]: Like, there is no difference.

413
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:39,306
[nm]: And that's why they'll continue clutching at the door, which is the whole essence of sīlabbataparāmāsa.

414
00:32:41,650 --> 00:32:42,769
[tn]: You don't know how to relax.

415
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:45,340
[tn]: You don't know how to endure calmly.

416
00:32:46,514 --> 00:32:48,125
[nm]: Well, yeah, you don't know, like...

417
00:32:48,120 --> 00:32:49,337
[md]: You don't know where the...

418
00:32:49,333 --> 00:32:50,180
[tn]: Where the problem is.

419
00:32:50,190 --> 00:32:51,920
[md]: You don't know where the problem actually comes from.

420
00:32:52,773 --> 00:32:54,773
[nm]: Because what happens if you let go of the door?

421
00:32:55,603 --> 00:32:58,540
[nm]: Your mind gets filled with the doubt, what if that door opens on its own?

422
00:33:00,617 --> 00:33:02,758
[nm]: And it's like, that's your practice now.

423
00:33:02,792 --> 00:33:03,489
[nm]: That's your training.

424
00:33:04,754 --> 00:33:07,763
[nm]: Developing your mind, yourself, in regard to the mind of doubt.

425
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:10,899
[nm]: That's why sīlabbataparāmāsa and the doubt go hand in hand.

426
00:33:14,053 --> 00:33:26,441
[nm]: So, by then accepting that the training is on the level of doubt, developing your mind in regard to doubt, not acting out of it, enduring it on the right level, not allowing intentional thoughts to crystallize, they're rooted in it, all of that...

427
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:39,988
[nm]: See, in order to accept that, you need to abandon your previous notions of the training being holding the door as tightly as possible and doing magical visualizations that will magically, somehow, miraculously remove the pressure from the front of my door one day.

428
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:41,234
[nm]: It just won't be there.

429
00:33:42,247 --> 00:33:46,712
[nm]: And you realize, oh, yeah, those people don't do the right practice because they refuse to give up the wrong practice.

430
00:33:54,754 --> 00:34:00,304
[tn]: yeah, you already opened the door, out of fear... you are actually on the other side, holding...

431
00:34:00,438 --> 00:34:11,550
[nm]: Well, I mean, in a way, the door is not open, but another way, you're not... Yeah, you're not really developing anything inside, because you're still very much concerned with the outside.

432
00:34:11,550 --> 00:34:18,259
[md]: As in, like, the thing is, if you were to stop holding it, the problem is, you'd just be opening it; you don't see any...

433
00:34:18,270 --> 00:34:20,000
[nm]: Yeah, you would be opening it.

434
00:34:20,403 --> 00:34:23,489
[nm]: Not holding the door means opening it.

435
00:34:24,100 --> 00:34:33,725
[tn]: So, it's a lot of pressure, you don't open it, and then... you don't even want to look, you don't even know about what's outside there... because that's...

436
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:34,754
[tn]: So, you just...

437
00:34:36,171 --> 00:34:37,820
[nm]: Wish for it to go away, yeah.

438
00:34:37,828 --> 00:34:38,849
[tn]: You just shut down.

439
00:34:39,040 --> 00:34:40,460
[tn]: Try to shut everything.

440
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:42,864
[nm]: Or just get into meditation techniques.

441
00:34:42,940 --> 00:34:44,560
[tn]: Yeah, just to ignore.

442
00:34:48,019 --> 00:34:49,241
[nm]: So, you still don't want to train.

443
00:34:50,407 --> 00:34:53,714
[nm]: You still don't want to train in regard to the existing pressure.

444
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:56,521
[nm]: You still want it to simply go away, not be there.

445
00:34:56,770 --> 00:35:05,485
[md]: You know, if you're sitting in your room and you have this, whatever, pressuring thought, now it's like, okay, let me just go for a walk to calm down or something...

446
00:35:05,497 --> 00:35:07,485
[md]: "But that's acting out of pressure!".

447
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:09,321
[md]: No, you can go for a walk.

448
00:35:09,683 --> 00:35:11,040
[md]: And you can...

449
00:35:11,264 --> 00:35:13,542
[nm]:  Well, it is. You could say it is acting out of pressure.

450
00:35:13,660 --> 00:35:15,988
[nm]: But again, not to the extent of opening the door.

451
00:35:15,988 --> 00:35:17,040
[md]: Yeah, exactly. That's what I mean.

452
00:35:17,220 --> 00:35:22,651
[nm]: So, by allowing that, by recognizing that, you are kind of at the same time seeing the difference.

453
00:35:22,659 --> 00:35:22,895
[md]: Yeah.

454
00:35:23,840 --> 00:35:27,040
[nm]: But by just doubling down now and saying: oh, that's pressure!

455
00:35:27,060 --> 00:35:29,165
[nm]: No! no! no! no! to everything automatically....

456
00:35:29,184 --> 00:35:29,750
[nm]: It's like that.

457
00:35:29,767 --> 00:35:32,251
[nm]: Wishing that self-cancellation on the inside.

458
00:35:32,575 --> 00:35:37,942
[nm]: So then, then, see, I can either cancel the problem outside of the door or wish for it or cancel me inside.

459
00:35:38,590 --> 00:35:46,537
[nm]: Either way, that's the presumed kind of pathway of resolution, which is sensuality and self-mortification in its principle.

460
00:35:47,333 --> 00:35:49,992
[nm]: So it's like, yeah, there is pressure,

461
00:35:50,020 --> 00:35:55,398
[nm]: I'm going for a walk, or I'm doing this or that, but I know for sure, I recognize it,

462
00:35:55,710 --> 00:35:59,752
[nm]: there is no confusion in regard to what extent that goes.

463
00:35:59,889 --> 00:36:02,841
[nm]: And yes, ideally, I don't want to be moved even to that extent.

464
00:36:02,883 --> 00:36:06,118
[nm]: But in order to arrive there, I first have to get used to this extent.

465
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:25,398
[nm]: So, go for walk every day, if it maintains you not opening the door, if it allows you to stay with the pressure, if it enables you to not allow, through the ignorant intention, crystallization of the images concerned with the outside, with sensuality, with your will, with acting out on that level.

466
00:36:25,771 --> 00:36:28,704
[nm]: So, it's like, yeah, I'll go for a walk and perspective remains.

467
00:36:30,003 --> 00:36:32,015
[nm]: Eventually, as I said, when you get used to that,

468
00:36:33,870 --> 00:36:36,358
[nm]: going for a walk will become too coarse.

469
00:36:36,864 --> 00:36:38,003
[nm]: You won't even have to do that.

470
00:36:41,081 --> 00:36:49,123
[tn]: Also, maybe like, whatever you do inside is like highlighting the actual door that you're not opening it anymore.

471
00:36:49,140 --> 00:36:56,670
[tn]: That practice, you know, that's the practice that is important, the core practice of not opening the door.

472
00:36:57,257 --> 00:36:58,730
[tn]: Whatever you do inside highlights that.

473
00:36:59,660 --> 00:37:00,468
[tn]: Yeah, yeah.

474
00:37:00,495 --> 00:37:02,038
[tn]: As a I'm going to do something.

475
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:04,179
[tn]: Well, let me just highlight the thing that I shouldn't be doing.

476
00:37:04,182 --> 00:37:04,419
[nm]: Yeah.

477
00:37:04,640 --> 00:37:06,335
[md]: As long as it's not that, basically.

478
00:37:06,339 --> 00:37:08,990
[md]: That's what determines whatever else you can do.

479
00:37:08,990 --> 00:37:11,036
[md]: As long as it's not that... and

480
00:37:11,060 --> 00:37:15,638
[nm]: And it's going to be, as I said before, it's going to be... sometimes it will be more obvious, sometimes less.

481
00:37:16,610 --> 00:37:17,455
[nm]: But that's the training.

482
00:37:17,451 --> 00:37:23,603
[nm]: And also the point is then to... which obviously, as I said, with the right instruction, hopefully you won't fall into a wrong view.

483
00:37:24,087 --> 00:37:27,001
[nm]: of then thinking, okay, going for a walk is the practice.

484
00:37:27,010 --> 00:37:29,718
[nm]: By magically going for a walk, pressure will resolve itself.

485
00:37:29,714 --> 00:37:40,053
[nm]: It's like, no, this is something you do on account of being pressured by not acting out to the full extent, but not being able to remain unmoved either.

486
00:37:40,590 --> 00:37:43,855
[nm]: So, you still know where the practice is, where the training is.

487
00:37:44,518 --> 00:37:59,611
[nm]: You just, as I said, when purifying the gold, you have to, for a while, put aside gold with the other impurities and can't possibly be concerned with everything all at once, because that will make you lose sight of the obvious impurities that you should have... could have easily abandoned.

488
00:38:02,476 --> 00:38:04,681
[nm]: Because that's... that's exactly the pathway people would take.

489
00:38:04,689 --> 00:38:05,523
[nm]: Aha! Close the door.

490
00:38:05,650 --> 00:38:06,403
[nm]: Pressure builds up.

491
00:38:07,721 --> 00:38:08,278
[nm]: I want to ask questions.

492
00:38:08,290 --> 00:38:08,811
[nm]: That's routine.

493
00:38:08,810 --> 00:38:10,255
[nm]: Pressure: should do it. It's just...

494
00:38:10,255 --> 00:38:11,577
[nm]: And then end up becoming no.

495
00:38:11,840 --> 00:38:12,230
[nm]: No.

496
00:38:12,388 --> 00:38:12,746
[nm]: No.

497
00:38:12,956 --> 00:38:13,306
[nm]: No.

498
00:38:13,596 --> 00:38:14,266
[nm]: I was no.

499
00:38:14,758 --> 00:38:15,893
[nm]: Well, I didn't even... No.

500
00:38:15,893 --> 00:38:16,563
[nm]: Doesn't matter.

501
00:38:16,580 --> 00:38:18,133
[nm]: Just just absolute denial.

502
00:38:18,130 --> 00:38:20,308
[nm]: No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no... but then it's like: why are you saying yes to that?

503
00:38:20,500 --> 00:38:23,893
[nm]: But then it's like: why are you saying yes to that then?

504
00:38:25,763 --> 00:38:30,118
[nm]: So it becomes very limiting, and very, as I said, completely unecessary as well...

505
00:38:30,834 --> 00:38:37,699
[nm]: And if it happens, when you catch it... that's when you recognize how much you learned, and whether the perspective is informed or not.

506
00:38:40,980 --> 00:38:46,255
[nm]: Because, you know, people would arrive, it's like, oh, well, no to everything, makes no difference what I do.

507
00:38:46,792 --> 00:38:48,750
[nm]: That would be the next jump into conclusion.

508
00:38:48,850 --> 00:38:55,253
[nm]: Because you've been saying no, trying to deny stuff on account of the pressure, that then led you to a view that it doesn't matter what you do.

509
00:38:55,638 --> 00:38:57,112
[nm]: It's all the same anyway.

510
00:38:57,459 --> 00:38:59,523
[nm]: It's like, but that's not quite true, isn't it?

511
00:39:01,489 --> 00:39:05,634
[nm]: And even if we take it for the sake of an argument to be true, what you do then?

512
00:39:07,600 --> 00:39:12,601
[nm]: If it doesn't matter what you do, why is then your next course of action going to open the door?

513
00:39:13,721 --> 00:39:15,946
[nm]: It doesn't matter what you do, so why don't you just keep it closed?

514
00:39:16,632 --> 00:39:19,097
[nm]: Oh, it doesn't matter what I do, thus I'll go back outside.

515
00:39:19,400 --> 00:39:20,944
[nm]: That's usually what it leads to.

516
00:39:21,687 --> 00:39:22,680
[nm]: Self-mortification.

517
00:39:22,704 --> 00:39:25,836
[nm]: It has to just revert you back all the way where you started.

518
00:39:26,327 --> 00:39:27,180
[nm]: What you shunned.

519
00:39:27,729 --> 00:39:31,904
[nm]: The bait that you tried to avoid, and not learn about or feel pressured about,

520
00:39:31,908 --> 00:39:34,224
[nm]: or ran on top of a mountain like a deer herd did.

521
00:39:34,952 --> 00:39:41,432
[nm]: Stubbed out and then just went back straight, not knowing the difference between what's the bait, what the threshold is, and where the door handle is.

522
00:39:42,110 --> 00:39:45,916
[tj]: So, you could dive into... it's not really sense restrain.

523
00:39:46,370 --> 00:39:49,302
[tj]: It's like a sense of deprivation.

524
00:39:50,370 --> 00:40:03,337
[tj]: But... or like take on austerities which are particularly... which are unnecessary for that... for what you're actually able to withstand.

525
00:40:04,506 --> 00:40:07,752
[tj]: But then... but you're... but you are holding them.

526
00:40:10,209 --> 00:40:13,333
[tj]: So, do you learn within that container?

527
00:40:14,186 --> 00:40:15,253
[nm]: You're holding what?

528
00:40:15,660 --> 00:40:15,916
[tj]: Like...

529
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:16,826
[tj]: The austerities?

530
00:40:16,887 --> 00:40:17,763
[tj]: Technically.

531
00:40:17,806 --> 00:40:18,606
[tj]: The deprivations?

532
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:19,226
[tj]: Yeah, technically.

533
00:40:19,714 --> 00:40:20,800
[nm]: No, you wouldn't learn anything.

534
00:40:20,891 --> 00:40:21,546
[tj]: No.

535
00:40:21,900 --> 00:40:24,232
[nm]: Because you're looking completely in a wrong place.

536
00:40:24,445 --> 00:40:28,289
[nm]: Even, as I said, you're emulating the right thing, seemingly.

537
00:40:29,211 --> 00:40:31,641
[nm]: Internally, it's done for completely different reasons.

538
00:40:32,689 --> 00:40:33,493
[nm]: No, and yeah, that's...

539
00:40:33,965 --> 00:40:34,735
[nm]: That's a good point.

540
00:40:34,740 --> 00:40:37,580
[nm]: The difference between sense restrain; sense restraint is not deprivation.

541
00:40:39,066 --> 00:40:45,504
[nm]: Sense restraint is saying no to the right things, to the extent that the pressure arises, and then train in regard to the pressure.

542
00:40:46,087 --> 00:40:47,047
[nm]: Don't shy away from it.

543
00:40:47,051 --> 00:40:47,946
[nm]: Don't try to deny it.

544
00:40:48,194 --> 00:40:52,773
[nm]: Deprivation, it's a view of if I say no to things, pressure won't touch me.

545
00:40:53,398 --> 00:40:59,177
[nm]: If I just blindly increase things I deny, I will be free from the mental pressure.

546
00:40:59,401 --> 00:41:03,302
[nm]: And that's as ignoble as engaging with sensuality, as the Buddha said.

547
00:41:04,380 --> 00:41:08,106
[md]: If I'm still touched by pressure, it just means I must increase the weight of the [?knot].

548
00:41:08,120 --> 00:41:08,708
[nm]: Yeah, I double down.

549
00:41:08,700 --> 00:41:10,990
[nm]: I'm just saying no to more things.

550
00:41:11,070 --> 00:41:12,213
[md]: That's what's missing.

551
00:41:12,213 --> 00:41:12,590
[md]: No.

552
00:41:15,318 --> 00:41:19,790
[tj]: Yeah, I've always been curious about this step from virtue and sense restrain.

553
00:41:19,889 --> 00:41:24,000
[tj]: Like, it's kind of... it's often just said, like, virtue and sense restrain.

554
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:26,963
[tj]: Like, they're kind of simultaneous, or like...

555
00:41:28,420 --> 00:41:33,291
[tj]: But, no, no, it's... yeah, it's quite clear, I think, that virtue

556
00:41:34,075 --> 00:41:35,896
[tj]: There's a reason why it's mentioned first.

557
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:38,579
[nm]: Well, sense restraint involves intention.

558
00:41:39,493 --> 00:41:41,089
[nm]: Like the sense restraint in the suttas.

559
00:41:41,085 --> 00:41:42,811
[nm]: It's not on the level of just saying no.

560
00:41:43,367 --> 00:41:47,794
[nm]: So, it's like the monk doesn't look at the sight that's provocative of lust then and then.

561
00:41:48,365 --> 00:41:50,510
[nm]: Which means it can be a different thing at different times.

562
00:41:51,737 --> 00:41:53,973
[nm]: Sometimes the same thing might not be provoking lust.

563
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,259
[nm]: That might not be the intention why you're looking at it.

564
00:41:58,350 --> 00:42:03,718
[nm]: So, but if you just adopt the view that, you know, the thing is judged by its content, that's why I must say no to it.

565
00:42:03,714 --> 00:42:06,419
[nm]: I mean, some things are obvious, always unwholesome.

566
00:42:06,499 --> 00:42:08,232
[nm]: And that's kind of what virtue addresses.

567
00:42:08,240 --> 00:42:09,108
[nm]: Things you don't do.

568
00:42:09,740 --> 00:42:15,085
[nm]: But the training in sense restraint is a lot more nuanced than just say no to anything you want to see.

569
00:42:15,100 --> 00:42:17,241
[nm]: It's like, no, it's why I want to see it.

570
00:42:19,417 --> 00:42:20,982
[nm]: Why the eyes go this way?

571
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:22,167
[nm]: Why does the ear wander again?

572
00:42:22,171 --> 00:42:26,930
[nm]: And then it's like, oh, now, yeah, I know that it's rooted in sensuality, in pleasure or distraction:

573
00:42:26,940 --> 00:42:27,958
[nm]: I say no to it.

574
00:42:29,500 --> 00:42:31,805
[nm]: But it can be the same thing that then it's not rooted.

575
00:42:31,810 --> 00:42:33,382
[nm]: Then you don't say no to it.

576
00:42:33,390 --> 00:42:34,841
[nm]: Oh, but it's still good to say no to it.

577
00:42:34,845 --> 00:42:35,725
[nm]: No, it's not.

578
00:42:36,266 --> 00:42:39,043
[nm]: Saying no to it when you shouldn't obscures the mind.

579
00:42:40,377 --> 00:42:42,411
[nm]: Removes the basis for training there and then.

580
00:42:42,838 --> 00:42:43,641
[nm]: So, it's like...

581
00:42:43,817 --> 00:42:45,215
[nm]: So, why are you doing it then?

582
00:42:45,432 --> 00:42:52,198
[nm]: Are you doing it to train the mind or are you doing it to fulfill some projected ideal of austerity and purity?

583
00:42:52,790 --> 00:42:54,144
[nm]: That's obviously very ignorant.

584
00:42:54,720 --> 00:42:58,796
[nm]: The difference between thoughts taking the center stage on their own, which is basically not the center stage,

585
00:42:59,238 --> 00:43:04,331
[nm]: and thoughts taking the center stage through your own allowance is the difference in your intention, nothing else.

586
00:43:05,020 --> 00:43:10,548
[nm]: Do you have intention to not allow them to crystallize, or do you have intention that allows them to crystallize?

587
00:43:12,610 --> 00:43:22,594
[nm]: But, you know, if you're not... if you're not being training in regard to coarser forms of your own intention, this discerning them, seeing them, be pressured by them, endure them, not acting out of them, it's like you're not gonna see this.

588
00:43:22,647 --> 00:43:24,720
[nm]: Yeah, see this, it'll make no difference.

589
00:43:24,797 --> 00:43:26,317
[nm]: It will sound like be here now.

590
00:43:27,714 --> 00:43:29,146
[nm]: Just focus on the present moment.

591
00:43:30,041 --> 00:43:36,278
[nm]: You're not going to see the whole trajectory of the travel in between, or around.

